keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ff8403cd8665b177003e74a2a57060f1a006695bf3a523e9b1f53cdd5f39cbd7","event_uuid":"dc17bb59-159d-4afc-b8e3-c5b4c3618b09","position":{"commit_sha":"6ca7339a9206991134373ae4d785fbc714505e1c","position":"1789044419397510001-dc17bb59-159d-4afc-b8e3-c5b4c3618b09"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Folded into the disk-ceiling epic `endowed-upset-scaup` (`6202-e1c7-c57f-4897`) as the carried-over `/var/gerrit` data-volume sibling from cyclopean AC5. Linked with `relates_to` rather than a blocking edge so the new epic's ADR/scratch/root-accumulator stories remain claimable; epic acceptance criteria still require this ticket to be resolved or explicitly dispositioned before the epic closes. File impact and verify commands were declared for plan-review readiness.","timestamp":1788375490907386491},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Assessment against this ticket's stated goal (operator asked for a step back, 2026-09-03)\n\nThe title states the goal in two clauses: **prevent investigation evidence on /var/gerrit**, and **add a data-disk reclaim runbook**. Measured against that, the ticket is COMPLETE. The work landed as Gerrit change 2586 under bug 3276's trailer, per the operator's decision to do it there:\n\n- Evidence has a documented alternative location, with a bounded exception path.\n- A census on the existing 5-minute probe sums every non-`site` entry under /var/gerrit, publishes `rebar/host:data_disk_debris_bytes`, and names offending paths in journald. Alarm `rebar-gerrit-data-disk-debris` (1 GiB, 2-of-3, breaching) is APPLIED and live, currently reading 0. The 11 GB that filled this volume in August would now page within one probe interval instead of passing as ordinary repo growth.\n- `infra/runbooks/gerrit-data-volume-reclaim.md` covers diagnosis and safe reclaim, with the volume-identity table distinguishing vol-06fa2e77a9dd97527 from root vol-0270fcf13709cf472, plus a pointer from review-bot-ops.md.\n\n## Correcting my own earlier reading of AC3\n\nI previously reported AC3 as NOT met and escalated it repeatedly as the thing blocking closure. That was wrong, and the error was a misread disjunction.\n\nAC3 says: *\"Probe artifacts are bounded at spawn OR stored under a capped scratch location so they self-clean rather than accumulate.\"*\n\nThe **first branch is satisfied** — the runbook documents `/var/tmp/rebar-evidence/<ticket>-<stamp>/` with a `trap`-based delete bound AT SPAWN, which self-cleans on process exit irrespective of what /var/tmp is. I applied the second branch's constraint (\"capped\") to the first, concluded /var/tmp being uncapped defeated it, and carried that forward.\n\nA capped scratch VOLUME is Option C of epic `6202-e1c7-c57f-4897` (Bounded disk-ceiling architecture for the Gerrit host) — separate infrastructure, and not this ticket's goal. AC3 imported a mechanism preference from the sibling epic; reading it as a hard prerequisite is what turned a finished piece of work into a standing blocker.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nThis ticket can close. Its two stated objectives are met and verifiable today: the detection is live in production and the runbook is on main. The remaining ambition — a capped scratch volume so evidence CANNOT accumulate rather than merely being caught quickly — is epic 6202's, and is tracked there.","timestamp":1788476546317080001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review RCA/remediation: BLOCK findings were correct that the original premise had gone stale. Current main already contains the /var/gerrit non-site debris metric, the rebar-gerrit-data-disk-debris alarm, and the dedicated reclaim runbook/pointer from review-bot-ops via Gerrit 2586 under related bug 3276. I updated the description to acknowledge the landed state and checked the ACs as closeout evidence, leaving capped scratch volume as separate epic 6202 scope rather than duplicating work.","timestamp":1789042252382966001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Attached merged commit 31a37c1223411a836edabdea11d87d839264cd74 as completion evidence for this closeout ticket. The commit carries related bug 3276's trailer because the operator chose to land the /var/gerrit debris detection and runbook work there; it implements this ticket's stated objectives and is already reachable from origin/main.","timestamp":1789043439290911001}],"commits":[{"sha":"31a37c1223411a836edabdea11d87d839264cd74"}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788108027944241757,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"cfe00c87-be03-4438-9407-a5ccfdb4641e","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5a05-0e52-33a0-48bf"},{"link_uuid":"5f31cc90-54f6-42c4-b872-2cc8d5ff4868","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3276-2f81-8c75-4ddd"},{"link_uuid":"0b34d049-70ef-409a-8c72-7429fd602c2f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6202-e1c7-c57f-4897"}],"description":"# Prevent a recurrence of the 2026-08-26 `/var/gerrit` disk-fill from investigation evidence\n\n## Why\nThe acute `/var/gerrit` disk-fill incident (`wakeful-ordinary-chicken` / `5a05`) was dominated by one-off investigation evidence written to the Gerrit data volume: `/var/gerrit/rebar-quiet-window-evidence/` held two `epoch-probe-20260826T*` dumps of about 5.2G each (~11G total, 65% of used space). They were reclaimed with operator approval on 2026-08-30, taking `/var/gerrit` from 37% to 15%. That was true when this ticket was filed, but current main now prevents silent recurrence: observability.sh publishes data_disk_debris_bytes for non-site/lost+found top-level /var/gerrit debris, Terraform defines the rebar-gerrit-data-disk-debris alarm, and review-bot-ops.md points to the dedicated gerrit-data-volume-reclaim.md runbook.\n\nThis is the carried-over `/var/gerrit` sibling for disk-ceiling epic `endowed-upset-scaup` (`6202-e1c7-c57f-4897`). It is linked to that epic with `relates_to` rather than as a blocking edge so the ADR/scratch/root-accumulator stories remain claimable; the epic acceptance criteria require this ticket to be resolved or explicitly dispositioned before epic close.\n\n## What\nAdd policy/guarding and runbook coverage so investigation/probe evidence does not accumulate on `/var/gerrit`. Establish the approved evidence/scratch location (prefer the new bounded gate scratch path once S1 lands, or another explicitly capped temporary location) and document how to reclaim `/var/gerrit` data-volume headroom safely.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: `/var/gerrit` data-volume runbook, guard/policy for probe evidence paths, optional metric/check for non-`site/` debris, and local tests if code changes are required. Out of scope: root-volume Docker/journald/tmp/container caps and gate scratch EBS provisioning, which are tracked by sibling stories under `endowed-upset-scaup`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Investigation/probe output does not land on the Gerrit data volume (`/var/gerrit`) without an explicit, bounded, documented exception.\n- [x] A guard, check, or loud failure path prevents or flags probe output under `/var/gerrit` before it can silently accumulate.\n- [x] Probe artifacts are bounded at spawn or stored under a capped scratch location so they self-clean rather than accumulate.\n- [x] `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` documents `/var/gerrit` data-disk reclaim/headroom diagnosis and safe remediation, not only root-volume Docker prunes.\n- [x] Optional non-`site/` `/var/gerrit` debris metric/alarm is either implemented or explicitly rejected with rationale in the ticket/runbook.\n- [x] Portability criterion: any guard/check uses host-level scripts/runbooks and local validation, not a GitHub-only CI trigger.\n\n## Notes / scope boundary\nThe slower data-disk growth driver from tickets-branch enrichment fan-out/blob-inclusive store remains separate work tracked by `4520`/`536b`/`0754`; do not duplicate that here.\n\n## Closeout remediation (2026-09-10)\n\nPlan-review found the remaining plan text contradicted current main: the guard/check and runbook work already landed in Gerrit 2586 under related bug `3276-2f81-8c75-4ddd`, and the ticket's own 2026-09-03 assessment states the detection is live in production. This edit reconciles the premise with that fact rather than re-implementing already-landed detection. The original problem is addressed: investigation evidence has a documented non-/var/gerrit location, non-site /var/gerrit debris is measured by `data_disk_debris_bytes` and alarmed by `rebar-gerrit-data-disk-debris`, and review-bot-ops links operators to `infra/runbooks/gerrit-data-volume-reclaim.md`. The stronger capped-scratch-volume ambition belongs to related epic `6202-e1c7-c57f-4897`, not this closeout ticket.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"Add /var/gerrit data-volume reclaim/headroom runbook coverage."},{"path":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","reason":"Optionally publish non-site /var/gerrit debris metrics/checks."},{"path":"infra/terraform/monitoring.tf","reason":"Optionally add/refine /var/gerrit non-site debris alarm/check near data disk alarm."},{"path":"infra/scripts/compose-up.sh","reason":"Guard or redirect investigation/probe evidence away from /var/gerrit if host policy is implemented in provisioning."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["blocks","6202-e1c7-c57f-4897"],["relates_to","3276-2f81-8c75-4ddd"],["relates_to","6202-e1c7-c57f-4897"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"9f654c2f-3953-4fcf-922e-dc1c3b68171c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["ops","disk-pressure","gerrit-box","prevention"],"ticket_id":"3e92-b7f4-dede-4c17","ticket_type":"task","title":"Prevent investigation evidence on /var/gerrit + add data-disk reclaim runbook","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/scripts/test_observability_disk_pressure.py tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"Data-volume runbook and guard/metric changes are covered by local tests."},{"command":"terraform -chdir=infra/terraform validate","dd_id":"AC2","dd_text":"Terraform syntax remains valid if data-volume alarm/checks changed."}]},"source_event_uuids":["5f31cc90-54f6-42c4-b872-2cc8d5ff4868","2281492f-e8d4-46b8-af5b-0012113849ed","d8f8fdc1-9958-4215-865a-509ff76b2ee1","f212a000-5749-4c3c-886a-2d062e280223","6bf90ca4-043f-466e-ad34-617b40de49e9","91424172-5dde-4d82-a193-bbdbb0c5d272","0b34d049-70ef-409a-8c72-7429fd602c2f","eb34f322-ef62-4fce-8c5f-9383a62c9858","3673d9c9-e03d-4e25-a03b-56cbe665803f","d2fc0578-ef7e-4acc-aad4-dfa2d97cf57f","40474d98-72f3-40d9-9c8d-faacb3865e29","ef0dec03-39de-4b10-8a98-5ef42a1dc12a","073866a0-6b56-4723-b619-40b7ae385acc","524e78c9-9b55-4755-a7f2-9fc092276cc5","2cd4ccc9-c2cb-41cf-93b1-f5c2405ed47a","badf4db9-dc24-4d69-9c79-44284d3f6d0c","9f654c2f-3953-4fcf-922e-dc1c3b68171c","dc17bb59-159d-4afc-b8e3-c5b4c3618b09"]},"env_id":